e  positives  that is we do not want to wake up the  device when no one is trying to talk to  the device  i'll just go through quickly through  some of the challenges  first and foremost privacy is paramount  we want to make sure that  false accepts are low uh you know  customer trust us and buy these devices  and bring in  and bring them into their households and  our  highest priority is to make sure that we  live up to those  that trust and customer expectation  because this is a far-field device we  have low signal to noise ratio  there's a lot of noise coming in let's  say from  background within the house like kitchen  noise and also from outside for instance  street noise reverberation  because you could have typically you  have  the sound bouncing of the walls and  other surfaces in the room and coming to  the microphones  in addition to the direct sound coming  from  the user's mouth to the microphones you  have competing speech  i have two young kids and they talk all  the time while i'm trying to interact  with alexa  and sometimes they actually win over me  in terms of the music they play  and you also have to be able to interact  with the device when the device is  outputting sound for instance if the  users want to change  a song or they want to skip a song we  need to be able to  wake up the device during those bargain  interactions as well  as with any speech recognition problem  you know there are  pronunciation differences also notice  that  the false accepts come from typically  come from background speech  and for households depending upon their  language  the false accepts could be very  different from let's say my household  where  we speak a couple of indian languages  versus let's say you know some other  households with native americans  um we need to  ensure that the backward detection is of  high accuracy and also low latency  what we have observed is if you  introduce several seconds worth of  latency let's say five ten seconds worth  of 